ers. It is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- **Norvane Utilities:** it plans 2027 capital spending up 12%, with the same focus on substations and transformers.\n- **Concentration:** Pellham accounts for 35% of utility orders at VLTX holdings and Norvane for 21%. So the two utilities with rising plans make up about 56% of that utility order book.\n\nTwo caveats:\n- These are plans, not firm orders, and they depend on financing. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, and equity markets have been less receptive. Whether the plans can be funded is the question n3 is working on.\n- I only have figures for these two utilities. Smaller utilities and the timing of orders within 2027 are not covered.\n\nSources: utility-capex-2027, vltx-order-mix and utility-credit.","ttft_ms":2549,"type":"result","duration_ms":14548,"uuid":"6c3f0b3b-05cf-4e91-946d-fdac240af33a","ttft_stream_ms":1689,"time_to_request_ms":756,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":14,"system_prompt":22,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":90,"input_hooks":33,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":81,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":97,"init_frame_send":47,"engine_pickup":27,"loop_entry":27,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":2,"autocompact":27,"request_announcements":144,"query_setup":26,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":23,"message_normalization":21,"client_creation":45,"request_build":24},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":482,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":183,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":203,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":130,"process_rss_mib_result":204,"process_anon_mib_result":122,"process_peak_rss_mib":217,"process_cpu_ms_turn":644,"process_wall_ms_turn":14548,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":53,"process_wall_ms_streaming":1207,"main_stream_count":3,"main_stream_event_count":105,"main_stream_chunk_count":13,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":53,"wall_ms